---
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// FINISHABLE — flagship case study.
//
// The organizing question, asked in the open: I own Ableton, a wall of
// plugins, and three hardware synths — why build anything? Because songs
// were dying in three places no product touches, and each chapter is the
// tool that closes one of them, in workflow order:
//
//   open        — the question (FinHero)
//   chapter 01  — KNOW WHAT YOU HAVE · the Catalog (ChaosToBuckets: twenty
//                 thousand files read by sound, deduped, and filed)
//   chapter 02  — PLAY, DON'T FIDDLE · Signal Studio (StudioChapter: the
//                 homepage instrument grows into the DAW; arm the found sound
//                 into three engines; the groove assembles on one bar clock)
//   chapter 03  — TRUST YOUR EARS · Richard (the journey: fantasy → the blind
//                 loudness trap you take yourself → the do-less dial)
//   epilogue    — the flip, then the whole finished side (Finale)
//
// One sound the whole way (Audio 14.m4a → "head to toe"), each state heard
// once. Honors prefers-reduced-motion; no autoplay anywhere; one audio stage
// page-wide (bench:play claim/yield).
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
import CSLayout from "../../components/case-study/CSLayout.astro";
import FinHero from "../../components/case-study/atlas/FinHero.astro";
import CSShortVersion from "../../components/case-study/CSShortVersion.astro";
import Chapter from "../../components/case-study/atlas/Chapter.astro";
import ChaosToBuckets from "../../components/case-study/atlas/ChaosToBuckets.astro";
import StudioChapter from "../../components/case-study/atlas/StudioChapter.astro";
import TheBench from "../../components/case-study/atlas/TheBench.astro";
import EngineDial from "../../components/case-study/atlas/EngineDial.astro";
import TasteLoop from "../../components/case-study/atlas/TasteLoop.astro";
import Finale from "../../components/case-study/atlas/Finale.astro";
import { round3, CARD_LINES, PALETTES } from "../../lib/finishable";

export const prerender = true;
---

<CSLayout
  title="Finishable — Jonathan Tollefson"
  description="I own Ableton, a wall of plugins, and three hardware synths — and songs still weren't getting finished. Finishable is the three-tool system built where music actually dies: a catalog that knows what I have, a studio that turns found sound into playable instruments, and a blind listening test my own ears can't cheat."
  ogImage="/case-studies/the-console/cover.jpg"
>
  <FinHero
    meta={[
      { label: "Role", value: "Designer, builder, sole engineer" },
      { label: "Timeline", value: "May 2026 — present" },
      { label: "Stack", value: "Astro · Python · Pedalboard · FabFilter · Whisper · Claude" },
    ]}
  />

  <CSShortVersion rows={[
    { k: "the problem", v: "Eight years of music scattered across four drives, iCloud, and a voice-memo vault — 20,279 files, no way to even ask what was in there." },
    { k: "what I built", v: "Three tools, solo: a catalog that reads files by sound, a studio that plays them back like a band, and a blind listening test that gates every mastering change." },
    { k: "where it stands", v: "The system runs on my desk daily; the first finished record is in progress. This page is the tour — the live tools are one link away." },
  ]} />

  {/* ═══════ CHAPTER 01 · KNOW WHAT YOU HAVE ═══════ */}
  <Chapter
    index="01"
    job="Know what you have"
    product="the Catalog"
    tagline="Twenty thousand scattered recordings, read by sound, named, and made playable."
    accent="cyan"
    flush
  />
  <ChaosToBuckets />
  <p class="door-line">Every bin, live, in its own room: <a href="/catalog">open the Catalog →</a></p>

  {/* ═══════ CHAPTER 02 · PLAY, DON'T FIDDLE ═══════ */}
  <Chapter
    index="02"
    job="Play, don't fiddle"
    product="the Studio"
    tagline="Where a found sound becomes an instrument, and an instrument becomes a track idea."
    market="Ableton is the finish line. Nothing owned the starting line — the two a.m. minute between an idea and a playable groove."
    accent="violet"
    flush
  />
  <StudioChapter />

  {/* ═══════ CHAPTER 03 · TRUST YOUR EARS ═══════ */}
  <div id="engineer">
    <Chapter
      index="03"
      job="Trust your ears"
      product="the Engineer"
      tagline="The last step: an engineer that has to beat doing nothing, blind."
      market="LANDR and Ozone ship one fixed opinion about better. This one has to earn every move past a null baseline."
      accent="green"
    />
  </div>

  <div class="eng">
    <p class="eng-fantasy">
      Version one was going to learn my taste from a million votes and become the
      best engineer in the world. That fantasy died honestly — under a blind,
      loudness-matched A/B it was overfitting a biased evaluator. What it left
      behind is a test I can't cheat. Eight rounds in, one rater — me — the only
      leaning that keeps repeating is restraint: the default is to do
      nothing. Take a round yourself:
    </p>

    {/* the caption now ships INSIDE TheBench, so /judge and this page can
        never say two different things about the same instrument */}
    <TheBench round={round3} />

    <TasteLoop roundId="r3-palettes" cardFile="~/automation/data/taste/jon.json" cardLines={CARD_LINES} palettes={PALETTES} />

    <p class="eng-lesson">
      That restraint, live on the dial:
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="cs-bleed"><EngineDial /></div>
  <p class="door-line door-line-green">Take the blind test yourself, any time: <a href="/judge">open the Judge →</a></p>

  {/* ═══════ CHAPTER 04 · FINISH — the record is the point ═══════ */}
  <Chapter
    index="04"
    job="Finish"
    product="the record"
    accent="amber"
  />
  <div class="cs-bleed"><Finale /></div>
</CSLayout>

<style>
  /* the door line wears the house chrome: the route's one mono token, the
     same rem size as .cs-foot-back, and the same brand-orange hover */
  .door-line {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 26px auto 0;
    padding: 0 24px;
    font-family: var(--cs-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    color: var(--cs-text-muted);
  }
  .door-line a {
    color: var(--cs-cyan-text);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
    transition: color 160ms ease;
  }
  /* each door wears its chapter's accent */
  .door-line-green a { color: var(--cs-green-text); }
  .door-line a:hover,
  .door-line a:focus-visible {
    color: var(--cs-accent);
  }

  /* the engineer chapter reads as one quiet column — a journey, not a console */
  .eng { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; }
  .eng-fantasy, .eng-lesson {
    font-family: "Space Grotesk Variable", "Space Grotesk", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1.8vw, 18px);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--cs-text-muted);
    max-width: 56ch;
  }
  .eng-fantasy { margin: 0 0 26px; }
  .eng-lesson { margin: 34px 0 10px; }
</style>
